-- title:
--   Chart table implies invertibility of the ideal sheaves F_k
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring, $t \in W$ and $e$ a natural number, and write $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,W\,t = W[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - t)$ for the chart ring, with distinguished elements `U t` and `V t`. Assume both `U t` and `V t` lie in the non-zero-divisors of that ring. Let $F : \mathrm{Fin}(e+1) \to$ ideal sheaf data on the scheme $\mathrm{Resolution}\,t\,e$, the colimit of the gluing diagram `glueDiagram t e`, and suppose the chart table holds: for every chart index $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,e$ and every $k \in \mathrm{Fin}(e+1)$, the pullback `(F k).comap (ι t e i)` of $F_k$ along the chart morphism $\iota_i$ is the ideal sheaf data attached to the global ideal obtained by transporting, through the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso` for the chart ring, the ideal $(V t)$ if $k = i$, the ideal $(U t)$ if $k = i+1$, and the unit ideal otherwise. Then for every $k$ the ideal sheaf $F_k$ is invertible: around each point of $\mathrm{Resolution}\,t\,e$ there is an affine open $U$ and a section $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ whose basic open set contains the point, such that on the affine basic open of $f$ the ideal of $F_k$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor.
--
--   This says that the prescribed components of the special fibre of the toric resolution of $uv = t^e$ are effective Cartier divisors, in the form of invertible ideal sheaves. It is used in assembling the special-fibre package [`MvPolynomial.CrossingQuotient.Resolution.specialFibrePackage_of_chartTable`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.CrossingQuotient.Resolution.specialFibrePackage_of_chartTable), where the Cartier hypothesis at a node of thickness $e$ is required.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_CrossingQuotient_Resolution_isInvertible_of_chartTable.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MvPolynomial_CrossingResolutionScheme
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_RelCartier

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false
open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

theorem MvPolynomial.CrossingQuotient.Resolution.isInvertible_of_chartTable
    {W : Type u} [CommRing W] (t : W) (e : ℕ)
    (hx : U t ∈ nonZeroDivisors (CrossingQuotient W t)) (hy : V t ∈ nonZeroDivisors (CrossingQuotient W t))
    (F : Fin (e + 1) → (Resolution t e).IdealSheafData)
    (hF : ∀ (i : Fin e) (k : Fin (e + 1)), (F k).comap (ι t e i) =
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (CrossingQuotient W t))).inv.hom
        (if (k : ℕ) = (i : ℕ) then Ideal.span {V t} else if (k : ℕ) = (i : ℕ) + 1 then Ideal.span {U t} else ⊤)))
    (k : Fin (e + 1)) : (F k).IsInvertible := by sorry
